# Territorial Kavu: "the number of basic land types among lands YOU control". Bot1 controls a Mountain and a Forest when it
# casts the Kavu on turn 3 while Bot2 controls a Tundra (Plains Island): the Kavu is 2/2, the opponent's types not counted. On
# turn 5 Bot1 plays its own Tundra: the types are Mountain, Forest, Plains and Island, a 4/4, a dual land counting both of its
# types and a type counted once however many lands have it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Forest
Territorial Kavu
Tundra
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x4
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Tundra
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Tundra.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Territorial Kavu.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Territorial Kavu.Power = 2
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Tundra.Play

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Territorial Kavu.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Territorial Kavu.Toughness = 4
